# Issue #177, through the real binary as an unprivileged user.
#
# v0.4.1 §34.4: "Any unavoidable global build MUST be visible in `explain`." `map` observes the
# whole space and `trace socket` reads every socket and every process's descriptors; the plan says
# so, with the §34.2 cost class, as text and as data (ADR-0947).
case: explain names a global acquisition and its cost class
env: NO_COLOR=1
run: |
  ono -c 'explain map'
  ono -c 'explain "trace socket 22" | to json'
exit: 0
stdout-contains: acquisition  global, moderate
stdout-contains: "acquisition":{"scope":"global","cost":"expensive"}
stdout-not-contains: panicked
